  "irVersion": 8,
  "notes": {
    "gate-rules": "Decides the exit gate's verdicts on files, test runs and places in production code.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.changedFile": "A production file that existed before the session, and whether the session changed it. A file that was not changed is always kept. A changed file is out of scope when this component's tests never use it, it has behaviour (not inert), and another component uses it; otherwise it is kept.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.partFile": "A file of a component this one contains. If it existed before and was changed, it is restored (and the change is a violation); otherwise it is kept.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.removed": "A file put in the sandbox at the start is missing at the end. That is fine for a file the phase may write (see SandboxFile); otherwise it was removed.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.sandboxFile": "A file found in the sandbox after the session, judged in this order. A hidden file (or the request) is skipped. A tool's file (type definitions) is kept if it is intact, and otherwise it was modified (toolchain-modified). A file that is not a regular file is not-regular. A file the phase may write is taken: in the wiring phase only the adapter, in the other phases only production code. Any other file that was not put there at the start is unexpected; one that was is kept if intact, and otherwise it was modified (input-modified).",
    "gate-rules.calcs.site": "A place in production code the mutation gate could break. It is broken (true) if this component's tests executed it. If they did not: it is broken if no other component executed it either, and its file is used by this component or by no other.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.tests": "Tests that must pass have run: ok if they passed. Otherwise failed, or regression when they are another component's tests run again.",
    "gate-rules.calcs.wiring": "The tests of the wiring phase have run. If they passed while unimplemented production code remains, they passes-unimplemented (the adapter does the work); if they passed and nothing is unimplemented, ok. If they failed because of an error other than the unimplemented marker, adapter-error; otherwise (failed for the right reason, or without an error), ok."
  },
  "root": "gate-rules",
  "sorts": []
